The insecure record of an account with an empty password is as long as the secure one, not one byte longer.

The record is the secure one with the password replaced by "*", so it shrinks by the
password's length less one. With an empty password nothing is replaced, but the
subtraction is done in size_t and len - 1 wraps around: the record grew by one byte past
what was built, a byte of the stack in pwd.db (root's in the base system's own
master.passwd), different from one run to the next.

--- a/pwd_mkdb.c
+++ b/pwd_mkdb.c
@@ -628,7 +628,8 @@
 			*p++ = '*';
 		*p++ = '\0';
 		memmove(p, t, data.size - (t - buf));
-		data.size -= len - 1;
+		if (len != 0)
+			data.size -= len - 1;
 
 		/* Write the insecure record. */
 		if ((dp->put)(dp, &key, &data, dbmode) == -1)
